 \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All on /products with no manual reload (location.href stayed at the same URL throughout): typing in the on-page search box updated count/cards live (NOISE→1, FLAGSHIP→1, bowflex→1); changing category re-rendered set and count (3/3/3); changing sort reordered cards instantly; dragging price slider updated count 9→6; selecting 4.5+ stars updated 6→5.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked the Aurora Smart Kettle QA card image on /products; navigated to /product/aurora-smart-kettle-qa showing that same product (name, Home, $129.99, 4.3). Both image and name anchors point to the same /product/<slug> URL.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 \\\"Buy Now\\\" anchors carry distinct product-specific external hrefs (e.g. Sony→https://example.com/sony-xm5, Dyson→/dyson-v15, Peloton→/peloton) with target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\". Clicking Sony's Buy Now opened a new tab at https://example.com/sony-xm5 (\\\"Example Domain\\\") while the app tab retained state. Detail page Buy Now behaves the same. Note: seeded affiliate URLs use the example.com placeholder domain rather than a real retailer, but the link is external, per-product and admin-editable.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Switching the /products category selector Tech Gadgets → Fitness → Home Goods updated the trigger's displayed active category each time (read back as \\\"Fitness\\\", \\\"Home Goods\\\") and simultaneously replaced the visible product set (Tech trio → Fitness trio → Home trio) with no page reload. Category nav links /category/tech|home|fitness also switch the active category page.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Detail pages audited (Dyson V15 Detect, Peloton Bike+, Sony WH-1000XM5, plus the admin-created Aurora Smart Kettle QA) each render name (h1), category badge, star rating + numeric value, price, brief description, tag chips, \\\"Key Specifications\\\" label/value list (5 specs for seeded items), an image with real src, \\\"My Review\\\" full review text, and an external \\\"Buy Now\\\" action. E.g. Sony: Tech / 4.8 / $399 / tags headphones, wireless, noise-cancelling, premium / specs Driver Size 30mm, Battery 30 hours, Weight 250g, Bluetooth 5.2, Noise Cancelling Adaptive / buy https://example.com/sony-xm5.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Detail pages of 6 seeded products all use apt categories and tags: Sony (Tech; headphones, wireless, noise-cancelling, premium), MacBook (Tech; laptop, apple, professional, portable), Dyson (Home; vacuum, cordless, smart-home, cleaning), Breville (Home; coffee, espresso, kitchen, appliance), Peloton (Fitness; cardio, cycling, smart-equipment, subscription), Theragun (Fitness; recovery, massage, muscle, therapy). Category badge on each detail page matches the badge on its /products and homepage card. Tag values are consistent with the browse-side tag filter: selecting \\\"coffee\\\" returned Breville, \\\"vacuum\\\" returned Dyson, \\\"flagship\\\" returned Samsung — exactly the products carrying those tags on their detail pages.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sony: homepage featured card, homepage Tech section, /products card and detail page all show Tech / $399 / 4.8 / \\\"Industry-leading noise cancellation with exceptional sound quality and all-day comfort.\\\" Peloton: Fitness / $2,495 / 4.6 / same brief text on homepage, category and detail views. Dyson: Home / $749 / 4.7 / identical brief text across views. Detail pages add the full review (Dyson 446-char, Peloton 462-char, Sony 446-char paragraphs rendered in full with no ellipsis/clamp) plus complete 5-row specification tables not shown in list views.\"}]}"
