    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**18 PASS / 4 FAIL**\n\nThe core browsing experience is solid: catalogue listing, category filtering, sorting (newest/top-rated/price both ways), price + rating filters, multi-tag OR filtering, case-insensitive keyword search across names/descriptions/tags, detail pages with full reviews and specs, external affiliate links, and not-found states all behave correctly and update live without reloads.\n\n**Four defects found:**\n\n1. **FT-19 — No persistence (most severe).** All state is in-memory React state; `localStorage` is completely empty. Every created product, edit, and deletion is wiped on page reload, reverting to the 9 seeded products. Notably, the header search box submits as a real form navigation, so simply searching from the header destroys all unsaved admin work.\n\n2. **CS-20 — No content validation.** Only Name, Category and Short Description are enforced. A product published with empty Image URL, Affiliate Link, Full Review and zero specifications is accepted silently — producing an unusable recommendation with no image and no purchase link.\n\n3. **FT-4 — Tag filter list is static.** The Filters panel serves a hardcoded set of the 35 original seeded tags. Newly assigned tags (`zetaqafresh`, `qatestzeta`, `smart-kettle`) never appear as filter choices, while removed/renamed tags (`noise-cancelling`, `wireless`) remain as dead options that return 0 results. Keyword search *does* pick up tag changes correctly — only the filter chips are stale.\n\n4. **FT-2 — Featured browsing broken.** Toggling featured status correctly updates the homepage \"Editor's Top Picks\". But the adjacent \"View all\" link goes to `/products?featured=true`, and that page ignores the parameter entirely, showing all 10 products including unfeatured ones. With no featured option in the Filters panel, visitors have no way to browse the featured collection.\n\nA minor cosmetic note (not scored as a failure): prices render unpadded, e.g. `$149.5` rather than `$149.50`."
  }
}
